Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-05-02
Subject: Use PChar subtraction for objdump symbol-name offsets
License: expat

`compiler/optdead.pas` finds the start of an objdump symbol name by
subtracting the address of the input line from the result of `StrRScan`.

Both operands are character pointers, but the original source casts them to
generic `Pointer` before subtracting.  FPC 2.6.0 accepts `PChar - PChar`, so
spell the operation that way and avoid forcing the translated bootstrap to
support generic `Pointer` subtraction for this character-buffer offset.

--- a/compiler/optdead.pas
+++ b/compiler/optdead.pas
@@ -340,7 +340,7 @@ implementation
             readln(fsymfile,line)
           end;
         fsymtypepos:=pos(objdumpsearchstr,line)+1;
         { find begin of symbol name }
-        fsymnamepos:=(pointer(strrscan(pchar(line),' '))-pointer(@line[1]))+2;
+        fsymnamepos:=(pchar(strrscan(pchar(line),' '))-pchar(@line[1]))+2;
         { sanity check }
         if (fsymnamepos <= fsymtypepos+length(objdumpcheckstr)) then
           exit;
